  "about": {
    "lede": "A working farm on the ridge above Pokhara, where the kitchen starts in the garden.",
    "paragraphs": [
      "We sit in Astam, a hillside village in Machhapuchhre-6, up in the terraces north-west of Pokhara. The dining terrace looks straight across at Annapurna South, Hiunchuli and the fishtail ridge of Machhapuchhre. On clear mornings the peaks catch the light well before the valley does.",
      "Most of what reaches your plate grew a short walk from it. Millet and corn for the dhido, greens for the curry, herbs for the tea, milk from the shed below the orchard. What we cannot grow ourselves, we buy from neighbours in the village.",
      "The lodge is run by people who live here. Everything is cooked to order and nothing waits under a lamp, so dal bhat takes the time dal bhat takes. Tell us what you would rather not eat and we will cook around it."
    ],
    "highlights": [
      {
        "title": "Grown here",
        "text": "Vegetables, millet, herbs and milk come from our own land and from families in Astam."
      },
      {
        "title": "Cooked to order",
        "text": "Allow a little time, especially for dal bhat, dhido and anything from the specials list."
      },
      {
        "title": "Facing the range",
        "text": "Annapurna South, Hiunchuli and Machhapuchhre sit directly across the valley from the terrace."
      },
      {
        "title": "Beyond the kitchen",
        "text": "Yoga, meditation, reiki and reflexology can be arranged through reception."
      }
    ]
  },
